---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service ✦ Dosezy Comprehensive Legal Protections">
	<Header />
	<main class="flex-grow pt-28 sm:pt-32 pb-16 bg-[#030407] bg-grid-pattern">
		<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
			
			<!-- Header -->
			<div class="mb-10">
				<span class="px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-300 border border-sky-500/20">
					LEGAL AGREEMENT & TERMS OF USE
				</span>
				<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white font-display tracking-tight">
					Terms of Service
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-3 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-400">
					Effective Date: September 7, 2026 | Document Revision 2.4
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Main Container Card -->
			<div class="vercel-card p-6 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-[#0a0c10]/95 space-y-8">
				
				<!-- Highlight Banner -->
				<div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-sky-500/10 border border-sky-500/30 text-sky-200 text-xs leading-relaxed flex items-start space-x-3">
					<span class="text-lg shrink-0">📜</span>
					<div class="space-y-1">
						<strong class="font-bold text-white">Legal Protection & Open Source Notice:</strong>
						<p>Dosezy is an open-source, local-first software utility published under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0). By downloading, building, installing, or using Dosezy, you explicitly agree that the software is provided "AS IS" without warranties of any kind, and you release the lead maintainers, developers, and contributors from all liability regarding medication adherence, health outcomes, or data loss.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Legal Clauses -->
				<div class="space-y-8 text-xs text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/10 pt-8">
					
					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">01.</span>
							<span>Acceptance of Terms & License Scope</span>
						</h2>
						<p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") constitute a legally binding agreement between you ("User" or "you") and the developers, maintainers, and contributors of the Dosezy project ("Dosezy", "we", "us", or "our"). These Terms govern your use of the Dosezy Android application, iOS client components, Docker Self-Hosted Server Node, Caregiver Cloud portal, and related documentation.</p>
						<p>The core Dosezy codebase is licensed under the <strong>GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)</strong>. You may inspect, modify, fork, and distribute the source code strictly in compliance with the GPL-3.0 license terms. However, your deployment and operational use of any version of Dosezy remains subject to these Terms.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">02.</span>
							<span>Software Status & Medical Disclaimer</span>
						</h2>
						<p><strong>DOSEZY IS NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE AND DOES NOT PROVIDE MEDICAL ADVICE.</strong></p>
						<p>Dosezy is designed strictly as a self-managed digital scheduling tool to assist individuals in organizing personal medication reminders. Dosezy has not been evaluated, approved, or cleared by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), European Medicines Agency (EMA), or any other regulatory health authority. Dosezy does not provide clinical diagnosis, pharmaceutical advice, drug interaction verification, or treatment recommendations.</p>
						<p>You acknowledge that Dosezy is not a replacement for professional healthcare providers, licensed pharmacists, or official prescription instructions. You are solely responsible for verifying that all schedules, dosages, drug names, and alarm configurations entered into Dosezy accurately reflect your official medical prescriptions.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">03.</span>
							<span>Disclaimer of Warranties ("AS IS" & "AS AVAILABLE")</span>
						</h2>
						<p>TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE DOSEZY SOFTWARE, WEBSITE, CLOUD SERVICES, AND DOCUMENTATION ARE PROVIDED STRICTLY ON AN <strong>"AS IS"</strong> AND <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong> BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, STATUTORY, OR OTHERWISE.</p>
						<p>DOSEZY AND ITS DEVELOPERS EXPRESSLY DISCLAIM ALL WARRANTIES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, ACCURACY, AND QUIET ENJOYMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT:</p>
						<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-neutral-400">
							<li>THE SOFTWARE WILL MEET YOUR SPECIFIC HEALTH OR TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS;</li>
							<li>THE OPERATION OF THE SOFTWARE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, TIMELY, SECURE, OR ERROR-FREE;</li>
							<li>NOTIFICATION ALARMS WILL TRIGGER WITHOUT OS-LEVEL BATTERY OPTIMIZATION INTERFERENCE;</li>
							<li>DATA STORED ON LOCAL HARDWARE OR TRANSMITTED VIA OPTIONAL CLOUD SYNC WILL NEVER SUFFER LOSS, CORRUPTION, OR DELAY.</li>
						</ul>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">04.</span>
							<span>Limitation of Liability</span>
						</h2>
						<p>UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES SHALL DOSEZY, ITS LEAD MAINTAINER (SAAD), DEVELOPERS, CONTRIBUTORS, OR AFFILIATES BE LIABLE TO YOU OR ANY THIRD PARTY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, PUNITIVE, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES WHATSOEVER.</p>
						<p>THIS LIMITATION INCLUDES, WITHOUT LIMITATION, DAMAGES FOR PERSONAL INJURY, WRONGFUL DEATH, MISSED MEDICATION DOSES, ADVERSE MEDICAL EVENTS, HEALTH COMPLICATIONS, LOSS OF PROFITS, LOSS OF DATA, DEVICE MALFUNCTION, OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OR INABILITY TO USE DOSEZY, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.</p>
						<p>IF ANY JURISDICTION DOES NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF LIABILITY FOR CONSEQUENTIAL OR INCIDENTAL DAMAGES, DOSEZY'S TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ALL CLAIMS SHALL BE STRICTLY LIMITED TO THE GREATER OF **$0.00 USD** OR THE EXACT AMOUNT PAID BY YOU TO DOSEZY FOR MANAGED CLOUD SERVICES IN THE PRECEDING TWELVE (12) MONTHS.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">05.</span>
							<span>User Data Sovereignty & Operating System Limitations</span>
						</h2>
						<p>Dosezy operates on a 100% local-first architectural model. All medication schedules, logs, and personal notes remain stored locally in your device's SQLite Room database. Consequently:</p>
						<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-neutral-400">
							<li>You are solely responsible for creating regular data backups using Dosezy's JSON export feature.</li>
							<li>Dosezy is not liable for data loss caused by OS reboots, device factory resets, storage corruption, or app uninstallation.</li>
							<li>You acknowledge that mobile operating systems (Android, iOS) enforce aggressive background task killers (such as Android Doze mode or manufacturer battery managers) that may delay or suppress alarm notifications. You agree to exclude Dosezy from battery optimization settings manually on your device.</li>
						</ul>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">06.</span>
							<span>Indemnification</span>
						</h2>
						<p>You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless Dosezy, its lead maintainer (Saad), developers, contributors, agents, and licensors from and against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, costs, expenses, or fees (including reasonable legal and attorneys' fees) resulting from or arising out of:</p>
						<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-neutral-400">
							<li>Your violation of these Terms;</li>
							<li>Your reliance on Dosezy for critical medication scheduling or emergency health situations;</li>
							<li>Inaccurate, incomplete, or erroneous data entered into the application by you or a caregiver;</li>
							<li>Your violation of any third-party right, including medical privacy or intellectual property rights.</li>
						</ul>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">07.</span>
							<span>Cloud Synchronization & Third-Party Infrastructure</span>
						</h2>
						<p>If you choose to enable the optional Caregiver Cloud Platform or deploy a Docker Self-Host Node, client-side End-to-End Encryption (E2EE) is utilized. You retain exclusive custody of your encryption keys. Dosezy developers cannot decrypt your sync payloads and bear no responsibility for lost encryption passphrases or unrecoverable sync states.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">08.</span>
							<span>Intellectual Property & Branding</span>
						</h2>
						<p>While the source code is licensed under GPL-3.0, the name "Dosezy", the squircle pill logo, brand icons, and custom graphic assets remain the exclusive intellectual property of Saad and the Dosezy project. Nothing in these Terms grants you a license to use Dosezy trademarks or brand assets for commercial endorsements without prior written authorization.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">09.</span>
							<span>Governing Law, Dispute Resolution & Severability</span>
						</h2>
						<p>These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with applicable laws without giving effect to any principles of conflicts of law. Any legal action or proceeding arising under these Terms shall be resolved individually without resort to any form of class action.</p>
						<p>If any provision of these Terms is found to be unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that provision shall be deemed severable from these Terms and shall not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions.</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-3">
						<h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-display flex items-center space-x-2">
							<span class="text-sky-400 font-mono">10.</span>
							<span>Modifications to Terms</span>
						</h2>
						<p>We reserve the right to revise or update these Terms at any time by posting the updated document on this page with a revised effective date. Your continued use of Dosezy after any updates constitutes your explicit acceptance of the amended Terms.</p>
					</section>

				</div>

			</div>

		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
